msxml3: Do not indent an end tag that follows character data in MXXMLWriter.

writer_dec_indent() cleared the text flag before endElement() decided
whether to indent, so an indenting writer put a line break and tabs inside
every text-only element. MSXML writes <Value>text</Value>. makepri.exe's
dump output passes through this writer, and the Windows App SDK build reads
those values as file paths.

--- a/dlls/msxml3/mxwriter.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/mxwriter.c
@@ -645,9 +645,6 @@ static inline void writer_inc_indent(mxwriter *This)
 static inline void writer_dec_indent(mxwriter *This)
 {
     if (This->indent) This->indent--;
-    /* depth is decreased only when element is closed, meaning it's not a text node
-       at this point */
-    This->text = FALSE;
 }
 
 static void set_element_name(mxwriter *This, const WCHAR *name, int len)
